# Frontend conventions

When adding or changing the frontend, keep these shapes.

- Shared files in `frontend/components` use kebab-case. Feature
  components use PascalCase. Logic modules use camelCase.
- A feature `index.ts` exports only the component the route imports.
- Add an API client function when a screen calls it. Remove it when
  the last caller goes away.
- `pnpm format:check` stays in CI next to lint. Prettier is the
  formatting source.
- Add a primitive in `frontend/components/ui` when a screen needs it.
  Do not leave a generated primitive that nothing imports.

```tsx
export { CategoriesClient } from "./CategoriesClient";
```

Money display is separate, and it applies only in this repo. See
`.cursor/rules/frontend-currency.mdc`.
